## Tests — organised by ownership

Read `test-by-ownership`. Five layers, and the cardinal rule is **one property of a
behaviour, at one layer**:

| Layer | Owns |
|---|---|
| Logic | the functional core, in isolation |
| Composition | several units of one capability, with in-memory adapters |
| Adapter Contract | one adapter against the real thing it adapts |
| Integration Boundary | one seam, both sides |
| Journey | one user path, end to end |

A behaviour asserted at two layers is a behaviour you will change in two places. Port and
Adapter run the **same** suite, or the in-memory one you develop against is not the thing
you deploy.

**Environment Blocked ≠ Test Failed.** A test that could not run because the environment was
unavailable is reported as blocked, by name, and never as a pass.

**In this repository:** `{{test}}`.

