## Defensive patterns

Read `implement-with-defensive-patterns`. Composition over inheritance; security shifted
left rather than reviewed at the end; every cross-process path emitting structured logs with
a correlation id, plus latency, throughput and error metrics. Dependencies arrive through
Ports, so the thing under test can be given a different world.

`scripts/check-resilient-boundary.sh`, `check-observability-at-seams.sh`,
`check-config-externalized.sh` and `check-stateless-request-path.sh` check the parts of this
that are structural. They are warn-first for the same reason the seam gate is.

